# The failover sweep's ratchet (ADR-0055 §11): every cell of the base
# catalogue that fails today, at either sync level, with the decision section
# that owns its correction and its cause, and each test's count of cells in
# the Guaranteed tier. A change that makes a cell pass removes its line; a new
# failure is never added without its owner. The list only shrinks, and a
# Guaranteed count never falls (a rise is recorded here).
#
# The owner is read from the finding: a request or final a copy sends without
# the record of what the dead owner sent, a request into a dialog the other
# copy ended, and the non-2xx a copy owes a caller the dead primary answered
# §4; a deviation no row of the window table covers, or a Guaranteed cell
# that fires a row, §11; a PRACK, an owed ACK or an in-dialog request left
# unanswered §2; a 2xx repeat routed through the other owner §8; and any
# other finding of a split cell §7.

# The Guaranteed cells of each test.
guaranteed basic/applied/backup-killed 18
guaranteed basic/applied/primary-killed 18
guaranteed forked/applied/backup-killed 24
guaranteed forked/applied/primary-killed 24
guaranteed info-x-bye/applied/backup-killed 18
guaranteed info-x-bye/applied/primary-killed 18
guaranteed info/applied/backup-killed 24
guaranteed info/applied/primary-killed 24
guaranteed keepalive/applied/backup-killed 57
guaranteed keepalive/applied/primary-killed 57
guaranteed media-leg/applied/backup-killed 27
guaranteed media-leg/applied/primary-killed 27
guaranteed prack/applied/backup-killed 24
guaranteed prack/applied/primary-killed 24
guaranteed refer-x-bye/applied/backup-killed 27
guaranteed refer-x-bye/applied/primary-killed 27
guaranteed refer/applied/backup-killed 45
guaranteed refer/applied/primary-killed 45
guaranteed reinvite-x-bye/applied/backup-killed 18
guaranteed reinvite-x-bye/applied/primary-killed 18
guaranteed reinvite/applied/backup-killed 27
guaranteed reinvite/applied/primary-killed 27
guaranteed update-x-bye/applied/backup-killed 18
guaranteed update-x-bye/applied/primary-killed 18
guaranteed update/applied/backup-killed 24
guaranteed update/applied/primary-killed 24

# applied: the Guaranteed cells that fire a row.
basic/applied/primary-killed/t1-logged ADR-0055 §11  # guaranteed: W-clean-end, the caller ended cleanly: killed at the creation turn's logged sub-point, the backup never held the call
